This licence covers what is actually ours in this repository: the setup
script, the host runtime, the tools, the analysis summaries and the
documentation. It does NOT cover Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic itself.

Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic is (c) 2003 BioWare / LucasArts, and
Star Wars is a trademark of Lucasfilm Ltd. None of it is ours to license. Its
executables, data, movies, music and art are not in this repository and are
excluded by .gitignore.

Two consequences worth being explicit about:

  * You need your own copy of the game to use any of this. Setup.cmd links
    your install as game/ (a junction, not a copy); the pipeline reads it
    from there.

  * Unwrapped and lifted code is a derivative work of the binary it came from.
    Anything this pipeline emits into work/ or src/recomp/gen/ carries whatever
    licence the original carries, not this one. The MIT grant above stops at
    our own work.
